TCP VS UDP

TCP: lossless
    -handshake validates the source adress
    -all of nothing: if one packet is dropped, request fails
    -relaible, at the cost of performance
    -example usages: websites, text chat, email

UDP: Lossy

    - Fast, at the cost of reliability
    - source pelts destination with packets
    - destination does its best to process as fast as possible
    - example usages: DNS, video streaming, voice chat.